  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="aafd-4594-de52-1289" name="Trojan War (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>TROJAN WAR ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.8-9), for Mycenaean Greek, Minoan Cretan or Trojan armies (a Sea Peoples army can be made with modification).
Characters: the army must have a General and may have up to a quarter of its points in Hero characters, including the General. Chariotry up to half; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter.
Archers mixed into spearmen units: one archer for every three spearmen (25%), counted as part of the spearmen unit, all shielded (not modelled: all models in a unit are equipped alike).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
